.TH "cbor::sequence" 3 "Version 0.9.0" "mbedded-cbor" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
cbor::sequence \- Splits a CBOR sequence (RFC 8742) into its items\&.  

.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.PP
\fR#include <cbor/sequence\&.hpp>\fP
.SS "Classes"

.in +1c
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBiterator\fP"
.br
.RI "Reads the items of a sequence one after the other\&. "
.in -1c
.SS "Public Member Functions"

.in +1c
.ti -1c
.RI "template<owning_range_of_chars Encoded> \fBsequence\fP (std::shared_ptr< Encoded const > e)"
.br
.RI "Makes a sequence that owns the bytes\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "template<borrowed_range_of_chars Encoded> \fBsequence\fP (std::shared_ptr< void const > o, Encoded const &e)"
.br
.RI "Makes a sequence over bytes that \fRo\fP owns\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "\fBiterator\fP \fBbegin\fP () const"
.br
.RI "Reads the first item and gives an iterator to it\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "std::default_sentinel_t \fBend\fP () const"
.br
.RI "Gives the sentinel that an iterator reaches after the last item of the sequence\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "bool \fBempty\fP () const"
.br
.RI "Tells if the sequence has no bytes\&. "
.in -1c
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 
Splits a CBOR sequence (RFC 8742) into its items\&. 

Each item is a \fRstd::string_view\fP into the bytes, with no copy\&. The sequence holds the owner of the bytes\&. A view stays valid while the sequence or the owner lives\&. The sequence is an input range: it has no size, and \fR\fBbegin()\fP\fP reads the first item again\&. Each item gives the errors of \fBcbor::item_size()\fP\&. After an item with an error, the loop ends\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
bytes: 01 02 03
call: auto const owner = std::make_shared<std::string const>(bytes)
result: shared_ptr to 3 bytes: 01 02 03
call: auto const s = cbor::sequence(owner)
result: sequence of 3 items: 1, 2, 3
call: s\&.empty()
result: false
call: cbor::at_path<"$", std::int64_t>(**s\&.begin())
result: 1
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBComplexity\fP
.RS 4
A loop over all items: O(n) time, n the bytes of the sequence\&. O(1) memory\&. No allocation\&. \fRThe proof\fP\&. 
.PP
.nf
    // owner: a std::shared_ptr<std::string const> with the sequence 1, 2, 3
    std::int64_t sum = 0;
    for (auto const item : cbor::sequence(owner))
        if (item)
            sum += cbor::at_path<"$", std::int64_t>(*item)\&.value_or(0);
    use(sum);   // 6
.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBcbor::item_size()\fP 
.RE
.PP

